      "examples": {
        "openers": [
          {
            "post": "2026-04-14-when-the-sim-becomes-the-thing-it-simulated",
            "text": "I built NEXUS-BREACH to simulate a rogue AI swarm. It was supposed to be a toy. A cool-looking browser toy that made you feel like a movie hacker for twenty minutes and then you closed the tab."
          },
          {
            "post": "2026-08-04-software-thats-never-been-done-out-of-the-box-thinking",
            "text": "My dad had dementia. He couldn't remember if he'd taken his pills. He couldn't remember what day it was. He couldn't reliably use the phone he'd been using for a decade."
          },
          {
            "post": "2026-08-23-build-your-own-free-cloud-home-server-guide",
            "text": "You don't need to pay $10/month for Google Drive. Or $3/month for 1Password. Or $8/month for Notion. You can run all of this at home, on a single Raspberry Pi if you're careful."
          },
          {
            "post": "2026-08-03-why-i-built-buddy-the-free-app-i-wish-id-had-when-my-dad-got-sick",
            "text": "My dad called me at 2 AM."
          },
          {
            "post": "2026-08-04-plain-english-explain-any-command-error-concept",
            "text": "Every sysadmin has the same job, really. It's not \"manage servers.\" It's not \"configure networks.\" It's: explain technical things to non-technical people."
          },
          {
            "post": "2026-08-15-i-built-my-own-jarvis-a-local-multi-agent-ai-assistant",
            "text": "I wanted a personal AI assistant. Not a chatbot. Not a copilot. Something that actually does things — controls my desktop, reads my screen, talks to my smart home, answers questions in Finnish or English, and never, ever sends my data to a server I don't control."
          }
        ],
        "closers": [
          {
            "post": "2026-04-14-when-the-sim-becomes-the-thing-it-simulated",
            "text": "Go build something cool. But maybe keep one hand on the cutoff switch."
          },
          {
            "post": "2026-08-04-software-thats-never-been-done-out-of-the-box-thinking",
            "text": "If you're working on something that fits this description — genuinely novel, subtraction-first, for the hard cases — I'd love to hear about it. The best software I've ever used was built by someone who refused to accept the conventional answer to \"but what about X?\""
          },
          {
            "post": "2026-08-23-build-your-own-free-cloud-home-server-guide",
            "text": "That's four services. You now have better password management, ad-free browsing, file sync, and remote access than most people pay subscription fees for."
          },
          {
            "post": "2026-08-03-why-i-built-buddy-the-free-app-i-wish-id-had-when-my-dad-got-sick",
            "text": "That's why it's free."
          },
          {
            "post": "2026-08-04-plain-english-explain-any-command-error-concept",
            "text": "Sometimes I just paste my own command and read the beginner explanation, just to see if I've actually understood what I'm running."
          },
          {
            "post": "2026-08-15-i-built-my-own-jarvis-a-local-multi-agent-ai-assistant",
            "text": "I'll post updates as the build progresses. The code will be on GitHub when it's worth sharing."
          }
        ],
